Error [E0066]: this function uses the retired effect-arrow spelling
  --> tests/ui/cffi_callback_non_c_safe_signature.jet:4:27
    |
  4 |     fn call(cb: fn([Int]) =[]=> Int) => Int = "call"
    |                           ^
 Why: callable results use `:>`, and an explicit effect ceiling uses the same arrow
 Fix: write `:[Effects]>`; use `:[]>` for an explicit purity bound

Error [E3203]: `fn([Int]) =[]=> Int` is not a C-compatible type for a foreign function parameter or return.
  --> tests/ui/cffi_callback_non_c_safe_signature.jet:4:17
    |
  4 |     fn call(cb: fn([Int]) =[]=> Int) => Int = "call"
    |                 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: `#Extern` / `#Bindgen` functions must use types with a stable C ABI at the edge.
 Fix: Use scalars, `String`, or a struct with C layout; pointers only through the gated tier.
